  "historical_output_text": " I used this morning walk to check out some of our city parks for ideas for an art exhibit on urban wildlife.\nMy feet padded softly across soft moss undergrowth and over crunchy autumn foliage in our favorite neighborhood green space – the place our dogs love best. But this time something struck home. A tiny, delicate orchid was poking from beneath a fallen befall. A single blossom – so rare here in a sea urban concrete, steel beams, concrete and leafy branches and trees.\nAt the same time the first snowflake of a coming bliz looked and I felt like an intruded visitor to this little hidden gem. I'd seen the little pink star before but this morning I finally appreciated how fragile it really looks, standing proud but tiny against such odds.\nMy mind began to play, wondering what this delicate blossom might be trying so desperately against all",
